{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>It is the burnt offering.</b> It is called thus because it goes up entirely upon the altar, and here there is a hint that a burnt offering is not to be offered at night; rather, it shall be on its hearth all the night. And perhaps מוקדה is a single form, or מוקד and מוקדה are two names:" "<b>And the fire of the altar shall burn in it.</b> And not outside it:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved ה״א as הא (האמת שבדבר / 'perhaps'); reading as interrogative heh makes no sense here. The grammatical point is whether מוקדה is one morphological form or two distinct nouns."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:45.419666337Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}